{"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/architectureguide"]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Understand the architectural patterns that make Swidux work correctly with SwiftUI’s observation system."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Swidux relies on specific patterns to ensure correct "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Observable"},{"type":"text","text":" behavior, efficient rendering, and safe concurrency. This article explains the reasoning behind these patterns."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"The Snapshot Pattern","anchor":"The-Snapshot-Pattern"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"send()"},{"type":"text","text":" copies stored properties into a local "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AppState"},{"type":"text","text":", mutates the copy via the reducer, then assigns back. This is required for two reasons:"}]},{"type":"orderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"@Observable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" equality checking."}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"set"},{"type":"text","text":" accessor checks "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Equatable"},{"type":"text","text":" and suppresses no-op notifications. Swift’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_modify"},{"type":"text","text":" accessor (used by "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"inout"},{"type":"text","text":") fires notifications unconditionally. The snapshot pattern routes through "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"set"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Cross-slice observation isolation."}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" Separate stored properties ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"var items"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"var tags"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"var ui"},{"type":"text","text":") mean a view reading "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.items"},{"type":"text","text":" won’t re-render when only "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.ui"},{"type":"text","text":" changes. A single "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"var state: AppState"},{"type":"text","text":" would invalidate all observers on every dispatch."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Because the stored properties are app-specific, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"send()"},{"type":"text","text":" cannot be provided by the framework — it must be written in each app’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AppStore"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"aside","style":"note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Explicit equality guards ("},{"code":"if x != state.x { x = state.x }","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":") are unnecessary. "},{"code":"@Observable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" already checks equality on "},{"code":"set","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Unconditional assignment is safe."}]}],"name":"Note"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Dispatch Loop Detection","anchor":"Dispatch-Loop-Detection"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin"},{"type":"text","text":" warns if "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"afterReduce"},{"type":"text","text":" is called more than 100 times per debounce interval. This usually means "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"send()"},{"type":"text","text":" isn’t using the snapshot pattern, causing cascading re-renders that trigger re-dispatches."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Reducer Weight","anchor":"Reducer-Weight"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Reducers run synchronously on the MainActor. Move O(n²) work into an "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Effect"},{"type":"text","text":" and dispatch the result back as an action."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Effect Threading","anchor":"Effect-Threading"},{"type":"aside","style":"important","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Effects run on Swift concurrency’s cooperative thread pool via "},{"code":"Task { @concurrent in }","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Blocking calls ("},{"code":"Process.waitUntilExit()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"DispatchSemaphore.wait()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"Thread.sleep()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":") hold threads hostage. If enough block, the pool starves and the MainActor freezes."}]}],"name":"Important"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use async alternatives: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"terminationHandler"},{"type":"text","text":" + continuation instead of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"waitUntilExit()"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Task.sleep()"},{"type":"text","text":" instead of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Thread.sleep()"},{"type":"text","text":", async file I\/O instead of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Data(contentsOf:)"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ArchitectureGuide","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"article","sections":[],"metadata":{"role":"article","modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"roleHeading":"Article","title":"Architecture & Performance"},"references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PersistencePlugin":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/persistenceplugin","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Coalescing persistence plugin."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"PersistencePlugin"}],"title":"PersistencePlugin","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"PersistencePlugin","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux":{"title":"Swidux","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Redux-style state management for SwiftUI with built-in persistence."}],"role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swidux","type":"topic"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Effect":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An async unit of work returned by a reducer."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"typealias"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Effect"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Effect","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Effect"}],"title":"Effect","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/effect"}}}